From: WL2GO
Subject: Answer DISCONNECT-while-disconnected with DISCONNECTED

wl2k-go's transport/ardop conn.Close() writes DISCONNECT and then waits up
to 30 seconds for DISCONNECTED (or NEWSTATE DISC) before giving up with an
ABORT, and Pat's fbb layer closes the connection twice -- once explicitly
and once from a defer. The second DISCONNECT arrives after the session has
already ended, gets only "DISCONNECT IGNORED" (which wl2k-go does not treat
as an answer), and the whole teardown stalls exactly 30 seconds after the
CW ID has finished. The same stall bites an operator pressing Disconnect
when nothing is connected.

When we are genuinely disconnected, saying DISCONNECTED is honest and lets
the host's wait complete immediately. The reply is guarded to DISC/OFFLINE
so FEC and ARQ-in-progress states keep their existing behaviour, and it is
only ever sent in direct response to a host DISCONNECT, so it cannot fire
mid-dial.

diff --git a/src/common/HostInterface.c b/src/common/HostInterface.c
index 0ba4eca..cf24365 100644
--- a/src/common/HostInterface.c
+++ b/src/common/HostInterface.c
@@ -629,7 +629,15 @@ void ProcessCommandFromHost(char * strCMD)
 			SendReplyToHost("DISCONNECT NOW TRUE");
 		}
 		else
+		{
 			SendReplyToHost("DISCONNECT IGNORED");
+			// A host that asks to disconnect while nothing is connected is
+			// waiting for DISCONNECTED (wl2k-go's conn.Close waits 30 s for
+			// it, then aborts). When we are genuinely disconnected, say so,
+			// so the host's wait completes now instead of timing out.
+			if (ProtocolState == DISC || ProtocolState == OFFLINE)
+				QueueCommandToHost("DISCONNECTED");
+		}
 
 		goto cmddone;
 	}
